  "preamble": "Loss of [s] without an attested intermediate stage. In French, s before a consonant was lost and the loss is often marked by a circumflex on the preceding vowel (Old French feste > fête). Proto-Uralic *s is zero in Hungarian (*sëne > ín 'sinew'), Written Tibetan final -s is lost in Lhasa Tibetan with compensatory fronting and lengthening, Nias lost all word-final consonants, and Puyuma lost Proto-Austronesian *S. In Armenian, PIE initial *s was lost in աղ ał 'salt' (< *seh₂l-) and ամ am 'year' (< *semh₂-).",
